<title>FRANCE: French state Charbonnages 1996 loss 4.68 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French state Charbonnages 1996 loss 4.68 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-owned mining company Charbonnages de France said on Thursday it made a loss of 4.68 billion francs in 1996, versus a loss of 4.17 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the 1996 result included 2.24 billion francs in restructuring costs, versus 1.78 billion the previous year. Turnover rose to 8.27 billion francs from 7.98 billion.</p>
</text>
